<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This experiment evaluates EduVerse’s ability to model interaction, moving from group-level networks to individual influence, and finally testing human–agent integration via the open interface.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T3" class="ltx_table ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Distribution of students’ network centrality indicators in the <span id="S4.T3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Dedication and Joy</span> lesson across environments.
Values are normalized to <math id="S4.T3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>; <span id="S4.T3.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Deg.</span> denotes degree centrality and <span id="S4.T3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Betw.</span> denotes betweenness centrality.</figcaption>
